{%- import "macros.njk" as m with context -%}
<h1>Budget explorer: what does the pension cover?</h1>

<p class="lede">What a pension leaves after a household's costs, from your own figures or a research budget. Why a pension can be enough for one household and not another is explained on <a href="/living-on-a-pension/">living on a pension</a>. <a href="/tools/">All tools</a>.</p>

<section class="tool" aria-labelledby="budget">
  <h2 id="budget">Fill in a budget</h2>

  {#- This and the first point below are shown only once the form is (W39). -#}
  <p class="js-only">Enter a household's income and spending to see what is left, or what is short. You can start from an example budget and change it.</p>

  {% call m.note("What the tool does not cover", 3, "before-you-start") %}
  <ul>
    <li class="js-only"><strong>Your figures stay on your device.</strong> Nothing you enter is sent, stored or put in the page address. If you come back to this page, your amounts and the result are cleared. <a href="/privacy/#tools">Privacy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>This is a budget, not a decision about benefits.</strong> The tool does not work out tax or any benefit.</li>
    <li><strong>It shows the present.</strong> It does not project future prices or pension increases.</li>
    <li><strong>Households it does not cover.</strong> It is for one person or two people who have both reached State Pension age. It does not suit a couple where one partner is under State Pension age, a household with other adults or children, or a person in a care home. The benefit rules for those cases are different. <a href="https://www.gov.uk/benefits-calculators">Benefits calculators listed on GOV.UK</a> can take them into account.</li>
  </ul>
  {% endcall %}


  <div class="no-js-only">
    {% call m.note("The budget form needs JavaScript", 3, "the-budget-form-needs-javascript") %}
    <p>The form is not available, because JavaScript is off or did not load. <span class="if-script-failed">The script for this form did not run to the end, though the page's other scripts did. Reload the page; if that does not help, <a href="/sources-and-method/#report-an-error">report it</a>.</span> The example budgets are set out in full under <a href="#example-budgets">The example budgets</a>.</p>
    {% endcall %}
  </div>

  <div class="tool-layout">
  <form id="budget-form" class="js-only" novalidate autocomplete="off">
    <fieldset aria-describedby="budget-household-hint">
      <legend>Household</legend>
      <div class="choice"><input type="radio" id="budget-household-single" name="budget-household" value="single" checked><label for="budget-household-single">One person</label></div>
      <div class="choice"><input type="radio" id="budget-household-couple" name="budget-household" value="couple"><label for="budget-household-couple">Two people</label></div>
      <p class="hint" id="budget-household-hint">Choosing two people adds a second State Pension field and changes the example budgets offered.</p>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset>
      <legend>Period</legend>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="budget-period">The amounts I enter are for</label>
        <span class="hint" id="budget-period-hint">One period for every amount, income and spending. If you change it, amounts already entered are converted to the new period, to the nearest penny.</span>
        <select id="budget-period" name="budget-period" aria-describedby="budget-period-hint">
          <option value="week">A week</option>
          <option value="four-weeks">4 weeks</option>
          <option value="month">A calendar month</option>
          <option value="year">A year</option>
        </select>
        <span class="hint" id="budget-period-note" hidden></span>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset>
      <legend>Start from an example budget (optional)</legend>
      <p>Each example is a research budget: what research found a standard of living costs. None is what people actually spend, and none includes disability or care costs. Loading one replaces the spending amounts below.</p>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="budget-preset">Example budget</label>
        <select id="budget-preset" name="budget-preset">
          <option value="">None</option>
          {#- A group per research standard, so each option can be short enough for a phone (W28). Grouped by tenure, and labelled from the first record, so this holds only while each tenure has one standard: a second standard for a tenure needs its own key. The household chosen above hides the other household's option. -#}
          {%- for tenure, presets in budgets.presets | groupby("tenure") %}
          <optgroup label="{{ presets[0].label.split(': ')[1] }} ({{ presets[0].price_date }} prices)">
            {%- for preset in presets %}
            <option value="{{ preset.id }}" data-household="{{ preset.household }}">{{ tenure }}</option>
            {%- endfor %}
          </optgroup>
          {%- endfor %}
        </select>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="secondary" id="budget-load">Load this example</button>
      <div id="budget-preset-about"></div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset aria-describedby="budget-income-hint">
      <legend>Income, before tax</legend>
      <p class="hint" id="budget-income-hint">Enter income <strong>before tax</strong>. Enter a benefit only if you <strong>actually receive</strong> it, and enter it once, here.</p>
      <button type="button" class="secondary" id="budget-fill-pension" aria-describedby="budget-fill-pension-hint">Fill in the full new State Pension ({{ "nsp-full-weekly" | fig }} a week)</button>
      <p class="hint" id="budget-fill-pension-hint">It is converted to the period you chose. The full rate is not everyone's payment. Replace it with the amount actually received.</p>
      <div class="fields">
        {%- for row in budgets.income %}
        <div{% if row.couple_only %} data-couple-only hidden{% endif %}>
        {{ m.field("budget-" ~ row.id, row.label, "", row.hint, "£", "") }}
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset aria-describedby="budget-tax-intro">
      <legend>Income Tax</legend>
      <p class="hint" id="budget-tax-intro">Enter the household's Income Tax here only. If tax has already been taken off an income figure you entered, do not enter that tax again.</p>
      {{ m.field("budget-tax", "Income Tax for the household", "", "Leave empty if you do not know it, and the result will say it is before tax. Enter 0 if you know no tax is due.", "£", "") }}
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset aria-describedby="budget-spending-hint">
      <legend>Spending</legend>
      <p class="hint" id="budget-spending-hint">Enter each bill at the amount you are <strong>actually charged</strong>. If a discount has already reduced a bill, do not also enter the discount as income.</p>
      <div class="fields">
        {%- for row in budgets.categories %}
        <div>{{ m.field("budget-" ~ row.id, row.label, "", row.hint, "£", "") }}</div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <div class="buttons">
      <button type="button" class="secondary" id="budget-clear">Clear everything I entered</button>
    </div>
  </form>
  <div class="tool-summary js-only">
    <h3 id="budget-glance-heading">At a glance</h3>
    <div id="budget-glance">
      <p>The result appears here as you fill in the form.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  </div>

  <p class="visually-hidden" role="status" id="budget-status"></p>

  <div class="result js-only" id="budget-result">
    <h3 id="budget-result-heading">No result yet</h3>
    <p>Enter an amount and the result follows the form.</p>
  </div>

  <h3 id="example-budgets">The example budgets</h3>
  <p>Every example is a research budget for a household in an urban area outside London. Weekly amounts, in pounds.</p>

  {%- for preset in budgets.presets %}
  {%- set s = preset.source_id | sourceRecord %}
  <details class="more">
    <summary>{{ preset.label }}</summary>
    <div class="scroll-x" tabindex="0" role="region">
    <table>
      <caption id="table-budget-{{ preset.id }}">{{ preset.label }}: weekly budget, {{ preset.price_date }} prices</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Category</th><th scope="col" class="num">A week</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for category in budgets.categories %}{% if preset.pence[category.id] %}
        <tr><th scope="row">{{ category.label }}</th><td class="num">{{ preset.pence[category.id] | money }}</td></tr>
        {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
        <tr><th scope="row">Total published by the source, not counting rent</th><td class="num">{{ preset.published_total_ex_rent_pence | money }}</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <div class="source">
      <p><span class="status">Research benchmark</span> {{ preset.tenure }}. {{ preset.housing }}</p>
      <p>Left out: {{ preset.exclusions }}</p>
      {%- if preset.note %}<p>{{ preset.note }}</p>{% endif %}
      {%- if preset.rounding_difference_pence %}<p>The categories add up to {{ (preset.rounding_difference_pence | abs) }}p {{ "more" if preset.rounding_difference_pence > 0 else "less" }} than the published total, because each line is rounded to the penny.</p>{% endif %}
      <p>Source: {{ m.cite(s) }}. {{ preset.table_reference }} Checked against the source on {{ preset.checked_date | dateText }}.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
  {%- endfor %}

  {% call m.unavailable("an example for every kind of household", 4) %}
  <p>We have no example for an owner at a minimum standard, for a household in London, or for a household with disability or care costs. The research we found does not publish them in a form we could check. We have not adapted a renter's budget by taking out the rent, because an owner has repair and insurance costs a renter does not. We have not updated any budget for inflation. Each example is as its source published it, at the price date shown.</p>
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="how-the-tool-calculates">How the tool calculates</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Every amount is turned into a yearly amount: a week × 52, 4 weeks × 13, a month × 12.</li>
    <li>Balance = income before tax − the tax you entered − spending.</li>
    <li>If no tax is entered, the balance is labelled "before tax".</li>
    <li>The tool converts the amounts you entered when you change the period, and says so. Loading an example budget replaces the spending amounts, and choosing one person clears the second pension.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><a href="/sources-and-method/#models">Full method and limits</a>.</p>

  <script type="application/json" id="budget-data">{{ budgets | budgetData | json | safe }}</script>
  <script type="module" src="/assets/js/tools/budget.js"></script>
</section>
